/.quarto/
/_site/
/site_libs/
/_freeze/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Rendered HTML never belongs in git. `quarto render` writes the site into
# `_site/`, ignored above, so nothing sitting beside a `.qmd` is a source file.
# The book's copy of this rule records what it is guarding against: thirty
# chapters were once committed as byte-identical duplicates of the ignored
# output, and because a full render deletes them, every later render produced
# thirty spurious deletions and invited someone to copy them back.
*.html

# The one hand-written HTML in this directory, un-ignored explicitly rather than
# by loosening the rule above, which is what `book/.gitignore` asks for. It is
# `include-after-body`: it colors the language tags, opens outbound links in a
# new tab, and keeps the two syndication categories out of the archive table.
# Without it the site still builds and quietly loses all three.
!/tags.html

*_files/
*.knit.md
/Rplots.pdf

# Staged by `R/copy-assets.R` before each render so Quarto can publish them
# beside the pages that fetch them. The first three are build output of a cargo
# invocation, the fourth is a copy of the book's stylesheet. Named here as well
# as in the root allowlist, because `blog/` is a public directory where a stray
# 823 KB binary would otherwise simply be committed.
/gog.wasm
/interactive.js
/view.js
/gog.css

# Staged from the repository's `images/`, where the README reads it too.
/images/pipeline.svg
